WEBVTT

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:18.680
The epic battle between
the Kingdom of Elfrieden,

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:23.640
which had summoned Souma Kazuya
from modern Japan to be its king,

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.610
and the Principality of Amidonia
had come to an end,

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:31.150
and a time of peace had arrived.

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:34.900
However, this peace would be temporary.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:41.120
The reason for this was that
the army of the Gran Chaos Empire,

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:44.160
history's greatest power,
was about to make its way into Van.

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:52.550
<i>"...Keep on going anyway"</i>

00:00:52.550 --> 00:01:01.600
<i>Our bond strikes deep into my left breast</i>

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:10.440
<i>We enjoy a fleeting happiness</i>
<i>after weathering one fog,</i>

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:15.450
<i>until our vision becomes obscured again</i>

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:21.410
<i>Bitterly betrayed, we grow</i>
<i>disgusted by our destiny</i>

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:26.290
<i>But why does the dawn still come?</i>

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:31.630
<i>We close our eyes and try to remember</i>

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:36.970
<i>the chance of stopping, of never meeting</i>

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:42.560
<i>From boundless zero to infinity,</i>

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:48.060
<i>dreaming is the heartbeat of believing</i>

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:51.900
<i>We'll move along alone and in pairs</i>

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:58.030
<i>Don't stay put; our small,</i>
<i>though by no means helpless steps</i>

00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:02.830
<i>will open uncharted territory</i>
<i>for each of us</i>

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:08.920
<i>Realize we will never again</i>
<i>let our dreams die on the vine</i>

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:15.710
<i>The tear tracks that run down</i>
<i>our cheeks are shooting stars</i>

00:02:15.710 --> 00:02:19.550
<i>We're going to grab hold of them</i>

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:24.100
"Amidonia in a Lion's Skin"

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:27.980
The evening is quiet, isn't it?

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:29.480
Yes, it is.

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:34.190
With Liscia and our son-in-law away, it's
almost as though the fire has gone out.

00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:38.570
But then, this is how it typically
used to feel before all of this.

00:02:38.570 --> 00:02:40.740
These days, the ministers,
the bureaucrats,

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:44.870
the Royal Guard, and even the maids
are working fast and furious.

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:50.620
And out of all of them,
our son-in-law is working the hardest.

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:55.920
I had no idea that the king needed to do
so much for the sake of the kingdom.

00:02:55.920 --> 00:03:00.880
Still, I believe that giving up
the throne to him was no mistake.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:01.890
Yes.

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:07.270
Will this... be what it takes
to change things?

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:15.070
It should be fine. Unlike that <i>other </i>time,
she is here from the start.

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:18.780
With the both of them,

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:22.280
I'm sure things will lead to a different
outcome than that <i>other </i>time.

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:25.330
Besides, it's not just
the two of them now.

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:28.450
Things are much livelier than
that <i>other </i>time, aren't they?

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:34.460
Ho, ho, ho, that they are. We have
ourselves another daughter now.

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:40.470
Yes, an adorable daughter named Tomoe.
One with fluffy ears and hair.

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:42.760
Ow...!

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:46.970
Was that too strong, Your Majesty?
Please forgive me!

00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:49.770
It's all right.
He's lucky it was just clay.

00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:52.230
If that had been a stone or a knife,
he'd be dead just like <i>that</i>.

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:56.730
Oh, man, I'm just no match for you.

00:03:56.730 --> 00:03:58.690
I-I wouldn't say that.

00:03:58.690 --> 00:04:03.490
Aisha, analyzing his combat potential
is important, so be honest.

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:06.620
So the adventurer party
strategy was a bust, too?

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:09.290
A real party would have a mage, though.

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:11.250
If your shield had
reinforcement magic cast on it,

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:13.750
it would have been harder
to get through it.

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:16.960
"Harder," but not "impossible," huh?

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:21.170
You know, I <i>have </i>apparently been
categorized as being a mage.

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:23.260
Hmm, I wonder if I got
some training somewhere,

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:26.970
could I become able to use
elemental or reinforcement magic?

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:28.140
Not a chance.

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:33.690
I've never heard of anyone being able to
use magic outside of their own attribute.

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:39.980
There aren't that many dark mages.
I've only ever seen three so far.

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:45.200
Three? Assuming Tomoe and I are
two of them, who's the other one?

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:50.450
Supposedly, my mother. She won't tell me
what kind of power she has, though.

00:04:50.450 --> 00:04:54.960
Oh, yeah? So Elisha can
use dark magic, too?

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:59.590
Still, it doesn't look like the powers
I have can even protect <i>me</i>.

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:01.170
Don't worry about that.

00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:05.340
Your Majesty, I will keep you
safe at any and all times!

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:10.060
A hero that has to be protected by
a woman just doesn't seem very cool.

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:14.140
Hakuya is looking for you, sire.

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:17.440
He says he wishes to discuss
the redevelopment of Van.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:19.560
So, the empire?

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:23.820
Mm-hmm. An imperial force
of 50,000 is on their way.

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:34.750
The redevelopment plans for Van
are finished. Please look them over.

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:38.000
Hakuya...

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:39.460
Sire?

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:40.630
You overdid it.

00:05:40.630 --> 00:05:42.050
Yes, sire.

00:05:42.050 --> 00:05:45.220
Ugh, there's too much
emphasis on efficiency.

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:47.260
If we're going to renovate all of this,

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:50.350
it might be quicker to just
build it from scratch.

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:54.640
I'm sorry. Just looking at how
disordered this city is laid out,

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:57.690
I couldn't contain my impulse
to improve the efficiency here.

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:59.980
Still, for the sake of firefighting,

00:05:59.980 --> 00:06:02.110
I think it's necessary to do <i>some </i>zoning.

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:03.650
For everything else,

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:06.320
I'd like it to reflect the will
of the people who live here.

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:08.950
The will of the people, sire?

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:13.660
I'd like the residents here to think
about what kind of city they want.

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:17.660
If we decide everything for them,
there's likely to be some backlash.

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:20.380
Judging by the mood in the city right now,

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:23.500
it's liable to become a city
full of avant-garde art.

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:27.970
A city of art, huh? <i>That </i>sounds
like it could be interesting.

00:06:27.970 --> 00:06:33.390
Van will be the city on the front lines
of Amidonia. I would not recommend that.

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:35.810
We'll just have to make it
a more comfortable city to live in,

00:06:35.810 --> 00:06:38.390
while still retaining its function
as a military town.

00:06:38.390 --> 00:06:42.560
What choice do we have? Come up
with something along those lines.

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:45.860
As you wish, sire.

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:51.820
Your Majesty, is redevelopment
even necessary right now?

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:54.910
And using the kingdom's funding, no less.

00:06:54.910 --> 00:06:57.700
Right now especially, Juna.

00:06:58.910 --> 00:07:01.750
The economy of Van is stagnant, you see.

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:06.420
We need to secure some employment
for the soldiers who have lost their jobs.

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:09.470
Little by little, things are
turning up on the streets.

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:13.220
It isn't enough. It's kind of like
when someone who is emaciated

00:07:13.220 --> 00:07:16.430
is finally able to eat, if I had
to compare it to something.

00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:19.100
We need them to get better, and fast.

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:23.150
And are public works sort of like the
feast that will make the city better?

00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:26.940
That's right. Public works
bring in new money,

00:07:26.940 --> 00:07:29.780
and that money further helps
to drive the economy.

00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:31.860
Unless that happens,
Van's economy won't improve

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:33.780
no matter how long we wait.

00:07:33.780 --> 00:07:38.200
I see. I now understand
Your Majesty's profound thinking.

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:40.120
What's the status of
the transportation network?

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:44.750
Sire, the military is doing everything
in its power right now.

00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:47.500
Service on the main road
is already complete,

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:50.590
and we are currently servicing
the roads to the surrounding villages.

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:55.220
Also, we have installed eight
bridges over various rivers, but...

00:07:55.220 --> 00:07:57.430
But what?

00:07:57.430 --> 00:08:00.430
I realize that maintaining
supply lines is important,

00:08:00.430 --> 00:08:04.730
but won't all of this be for nothing once
we are compelled to return their lands?

00:08:04.730 --> 00:08:07.770
That's true. Letting bridges
that were built by us

00:08:07.770 --> 00:08:10.900
get used by Julius and his people
grates on my nerves.

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:13.490
I doubt that will happen.

00:08:13.490 --> 00:08:16.280
Even if Prince Julius returns to power,

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:20.410
he will not allow any facilities built
by the kingdom to be used as-is.

00:08:20.410 --> 00:08:23.040
It would be a matter of prestige for him.

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:27.420
If it were me, I'd use anything I could,
whether it was Amidonian or not.

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:30.550
Knowing you, Your Majesty,
I'm sure you would.

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:32.970
If we're going to do this,
why don't we rub it in his face?

00:08:32.970 --> 00:08:35.220
How do you mean, "rub it in his face"?

00:08:35.220 --> 00:08:39.510
We put our names on the bridges.
There were eight of them, right?

00:08:39.510 --> 00:08:44.190
So then, the Souma Bridge,
the Liscia Bridge, the Albert Bridge,

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:48.020
the Hakuya Bridge, the Ludwin Bridge,
the Poncho Bridge,

00:08:48.020 --> 00:08:52.110
the Aisha Bridge, and the Juna Bridge.
Engrave one on each of their railings.

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:55.070
I get it. Even if the land gets returned,

00:08:55.070 --> 00:08:58.910
then since the Kingdom of
Elfrieden built those bridges,

00:08:58.910 --> 00:09:02.700
the anti-kingdom faction will
destroy them. Is that the idea?

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:05.040
The residents there will lose
the convenience of using them,

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:07.460
and blame the anti-kingdom faction.

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:09.750
If there are no objections,
the motion passes.

00:09:09.750 --> 00:09:10.750
Yes, sire.

00:09:15.590 --> 00:09:19.140
Well then, we should excuse ourselves.

00:09:25.810 --> 00:09:31.150
I suppose it will be difficult to refuse
returning Van if the empire requests it.

00:09:31.150 --> 00:09:33.780
I'm not going to change
the basics of my policy,

00:09:33.780 --> 00:09:37.070
but I doubt I'm going to be
able to twist Jeanne's arm.

00:09:37.070 --> 00:09:40.780
If we appear hostile, then this
will be a diplomatic failure.

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:43.790
Is it true that the hero summoning

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:46.460
was their way of being
considerate to the kingdom?

00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:47.920
Sounds like it.

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:49.920
How long have you known?

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:52.170
Probably around the time I heard
that the Empress Maria

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:55.380
was known as a "saint."

00:09:55.380 --> 00:09:57.840
A saint wouldn't do anything cruel, right?

00:09:57.840 --> 00:10:00.390
You put your trust in her title?

00:10:00.390 --> 00:10:02.970
Titles are given to people
because they're convenient.

00:10:02.970 --> 00:10:06.140
Where a saint walks, others will follow.

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:08.100
The world needs a banner carrier

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:12.320
for mankind to unite behind against
the threat of the Demon Lord's Domain.

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:15.030
Whether she wants to be it or not.

00:10:17.070 --> 00:10:19.660
I realized something when I met Jeanne.

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:22.950
The Gran Chaos Empire is nothing
more than a "mere superpower,"

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:26.290
trying desperately to maintain
their own nation.

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:28.540
Which is exactly why
we have to stay on our toes.

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:32.290
There's no room for carelessness or ego
when dealing with a tough opponent.

00:10:32.290 --> 00:10:35.550
That's true. We have to go
into this with our minds set.

00:10:36.970 --> 00:10:38.170
Enter!

00:10:44.970 --> 00:10:46.770
What is it?

00:10:46.770 --> 00:10:50.810
I bring word.
The Gran Chaos Empire's forces,

00:10:50.810 --> 00:10:54.070
as well as the Principality of Amidonia's
negotiating body, have arrived.

00:10:57.690 --> 00:10:59.150
It's time.

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:11.210
October 21, 1546 by
the Continental Calendar.

00:11:11.210 --> 00:11:15.380
At last, 50,000 of the Gran
Chaos Empire's elite forces

00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:18.630
have taken up positions
a day out from Van.

00:11:18.630 --> 00:11:23.180
With this force at their back,
the Gran Chaos Empire's general,

00:11:23.180 --> 00:11:29.270
Jeanne Euphoria, and Julius Amidonia,
the son of Gaius VIII,

00:11:29.270 --> 00:11:32.480
who once possessed Van,
and current crown prince of Amidonia,

00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:34.860
had marched into Van Castle.

00:11:36.820 --> 00:11:39.530
This is surprising.
I had imagined that this meeting

00:11:39.530 --> 00:11:42.740
would be encircled by
a large number of soldiers.

00:11:42.740 --> 00:11:44.740
It would be too unsettling
to meet with the two of you

00:11:44.740 --> 00:11:47.330
if there were an excessive number
of soldiers around, right?

00:11:47.330 --> 00:11:51.040
That makes sense.
Quite the daring gentlemen, aren't you?

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:54.130
I'm nothing compared to
a certain ruler who loses a war,

00:11:54.130 --> 00:11:57.750
and then runs to the empire
to ask them to get his territory back.

00:11:59.670 --> 00:12:03.220
Julius, the woman at our side
is a skilled warrior.

00:12:03.220 --> 00:12:06.680
Leave it to you, King Souma,
to have such a fine retainer.

00:12:08.140 --> 00:12:09.720
Why, thank you.

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:14.650
Are you not worried
that you might be killed here?

00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:18.070
I am here as an envoy of peace.

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:20.780
Why should I be concerned
that harm might befall me?

00:12:22.950 --> 00:12:26.870
It is nice to finally meet you.
I am Souma Kazuya.

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:30.910
I am Julius, Crown Prince of Amidonia.

00:12:30.910 --> 00:12:33.330
May I ask what your business is here?

00:12:33.330 --> 00:12:38.210
I'll come right to the point.
I want Van returned at once.

00:12:38.210 --> 00:12:39.920
Julius...

00:12:39.920 --> 00:12:44.090
The Principality of Amidonia is a
signatory to the Mankind Declaration.

00:12:44.090 --> 00:12:45.930
Its articles state that
any changes in borders--

00:12:45.930 --> 00:12:48.720
...due to military action
are not recognized.

00:12:48.720 --> 00:12:51.140
Have we violated that article?

00:12:51.140 --> 00:12:54.270
Yes. As such, in accordance
with this article,

00:12:54.270 --> 00:12:57.610
I demand the immediate return
of Van and its surrounding lands.

00:12:57.610 --> 00:13:00.280
How self-serving of you!

00:13:00.280 --> 00:13:03.990
<i>You </i>are the ones who invaded
the Kingdom of Elfrieden, aren't you?

00:13:03.990 --> 00:13:07.200
And now that you've been beaten,
you hide behind the Mankind Declaration,

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:10.450
seeking your land back by means
of the empire's prestige.

00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:14.160
The invasion of the Kingdom of Elfrieden

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:16.290
was an arbitrary decision
made by my father, Gaius.

00:13:16.290 --> 00:13:19.590
You took part in his campaign,
so you share his blame.

00:13:19.590 --> 00:13:22.380
For that matter, before we start
talking about returning territories,

00:13:22.380 --> 00:13:25.630
shouldn't you first apologize
for your invasion?

00:13:26.680 --> 00:13:33.180
King Souma is correct. Our position here
is to ask for your land to be returned.

00:13:34.480 --> 00:13:36.390
Despite the decision
to invade your country

00:13:36.390 --> 00:13:39.150
being an arbitrary one made
by the previous leader, Gaius,

00:13:39.150 --> 00:13:44.190
I am also to blame for being unable
to stop him. For that, I apologize.

00:13:44.190 --> 00:13:48.530
However, it is currently your country
that is violating <i>our </i>borders!

00:13:48.530 --> 00:13:51.120
I demand that you return our territory!

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:55.460
That's what you say, Julius,
but what does the empire say?

00:13:55.460 --> 00:13:58.960
We cannot afford to dismiss
the requests of our signatory nations.

00:13:58.960 --> 00:14:01.880
So what you're saying is that the empire
is demanding of my kingdom

00:14:01.880 --> 00:14:06.300
the return of occupied territories,
including Van?

00:14:06.300 --> 00:14:07.970
That is what I am saying.

00:14:09.680 --> 00:14:10.890
The answer is no.

00:14:10.890 --> 00:14:12.510
Wha--?!

00:14:12.510 --> 00:14:16.020
Are you out of your mind?!
You would defy the Mankind Declaration?!

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:18.100
I have no intention of defying anything.

00:14:18.100 --> 00:14:19.980
You...!

00:14:19.980 --> 00:14:23.110
I-I mean, as the ruler of this country,

00:14:23.110 --> 00:14:26.150
I must liberate my people
who are under your occupation.

00:14:26.150 --> 00:14:32.200
"Liberate," huh? Tell me, is that
what the residents of Van desire?

00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:33.790
What?

00:14:33.790 --> 00:14:39.210
Julius, on your way here, did you see
for yourself the streets of Van?

00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:45.460
I was born and raised in this city.
I know it far better than you do.

00:14:45.460 --> 00:14:49.840
Do you? Then what do you think
of the current colors of Van?

00:14:49.840 --> 00:14:50.970
Colors?

00:14:50.970 --> 00:14:54.720
I did see a number of houses whose roofs
and walls were painted ugly colors.

00:14:54.720 --> 00:14:58.940
Julius, would people who are feeling
oppressed under our occupation

00:14:58.940 --> 00:15:02.730
want to make their roofs and walls
more colorful, do you think?

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:05.110
W-Well, I...

00:15:05.110 --> 00:15:10.700
The color that I felt when I
first came into Van was gray.

00:15:10.700 --> 00:15:12.950
Not a single shred of individuality.

00:15:12.950 --> 00:15:17.330
But how about now? People can
paint their walls any color they like.

00:15:19.960 --> 00:15:21.370
Between Van as it is now,

00:15:21.370 --> 00:15:26.960
and Van when it was under your control,
which one is the better city?

00:15:26.960 --> 00:15:28.340
Why, you...!

00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:30.760
Julius!

00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:35.100
Aisha, remove your hand
from your sword, too.

00:15:36.470 --> 00:15:37.770
Yes, sire.

00:15:37.770 --> 00:15:42.520
King Souma, I would ask that you
quit trying to rile Julius up.

00:15:42.520 --> 00:15:46.610
I was only stating facts.
"To reign and to relieve"--

00:15:46.610 --> 00:15:50.820
governing one's realm and saving one's
people is what a ruler ought to do.

00:15:50.820 --> 00:15:52.700
They, who taxed the people
to death to fund the military,

00:15:52.700 --> 00:15:56.160
and made sure that they suffered
are the real oppressors.

00:15:56.160 --> 00:15:59.620
And whose fault is that?!
If you, the Elfrieden royal family,

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:01.790
had not stolen my grandfather's
land from him...!

00:16:01.790 --> 00:16:05.130
That's the Amidonian royal
family's favorite thing to say.

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:10.550
But the truth is, <i>your </i>country is the one
that has kept doing harm to <i>ours</i>.

00:16:10.550 --> 00:16:11.590
Hakuya...

00:16:11.590 --> 00:16:12.680
Yes, sire.

00:16:22.690 --> 00:16:23.850
What is this?

00:16:23.850 --> 00:16:26.150
A list of noblemen in
the Kingdom of Elfrieden

00:16:26.150 --> 00:16:30.150
who were incited to insurrection
by the Principality of Amidonia.

00:16:30.150 --> 00:16:34.240
Amidonia fomented a revolt,
encouraged fraud,

00:16:34.240 --> 00:16:38.790
and inspired them to be uncooperative
toward the royal family.

00:16:38.790 --> 00:16:40.370
My word...

00:16:42.410 --> 00:16:47.960
Jeanne, Amidonia pretends to abide
by the Mankind Declaration,

00:16:47.960 --> 00:16:51.420
while secretly interfering in
the affairs of foreign powers.

00:16:51.420 --> 00:16:55.590
And still they dare speak about
vengeance against the kingdom.

00:16:55.590 --> 00:16:57.720
It's the kingdom's fault
that our country is poor;

00:16:57.720 --> 00:16:59.930
it's the kingdom's fault
that our people are hungry;

00:16:59.930 --> 00:17:02.980
it's the kingdom's fault
that our people are suffering;

00:17:02.980 --> 00:17:04.730
it's the kingdom's fault
that our hard-earned tax money

00:17:04.730 --> 00:17:07.440
must be used for the military
instead of for the people.

00:17:07.440 --> 00:17:09.520
What are you trying to say?

00:17:09.520 --> 00:17:13.450
That it's awfully convenient. As long as
you keep beating the drum of revenge,

00:17:13.450 --> 00:17:15.570
you can conceal your own misgovernment,

00:17:15.570 --> 00:17:18.910
and direct the anger of the people
toward the Kingdom of Elfrieden.

00:17:18.910 --> 00:17:20.240
Damn you!

00:17:20.240 --> 00:17:21.790
Julius!

00:17:24.790 --> 00:17:27.500
I asked you not to agitate him.

00:17:27.500 --> 00:17:30.880
I'm sorry. I just wanted to make it clear

00:17:30.880 --> 00:17:34.760
that we are also fed up
with Amidonia's conduct.

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:39.220
Now, I would like to make a proposal.

00:17:39.220 --> 00:17:42.180
Could I ask you to leave the room, Julius?

00:17:42.180 --> 00:17:44.020
Huh?

00:17:44.020 --> 00:17:47.560
Forget it! Why should I be
excluded from negotiations

00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:49.270
to get my own capital city back?!

00:17:49.270 --> 00:17:52.690
It's a simple matter, really. There was
never any need for us to negotiate

00:17:52.690 --> 00:17:54.900
with the Principality of Amidonia
in the first place.

00:17:54.900 --> 00:17:56.700
What did you say?!

00:17:56.700 --> 00:17:59.530
It is the <i>empire </i>who is seeking
the return of your territory

00:17:59.530 --> 00:18:02.830
against the backdrop of military force,
not you. That being the case,

00:18:02.830 --> 00:18:06.870
this negotiation can be conducted
between the kingdom and the empire.

00:18:06.870 --> 00:18:10.590
Why, you... Are you saying
you won't negotiate with me?!

00:18:10.590 --> 00:18:15.550
Julius, would you allow me to handle this?

00:18:15.550 --> 00:18:18.130
The negotiations are
going nowhere like this.

00:18:18.130 --> 00:18:22.510
The empire does not wish to spend
too much time on mediation.

00:18:22.510 --> 00:18:25.180
I would ask that you
let me take care of this.

00:18:25.180 --> 00:18:29.190
That is... a bit of a one-sided
argument, isn't it?

00:18:29.190 --> 00:18:34.110
Then the empire withdraws, and you
are free to bargain as you like afterward.

00:18:36.650 --> 00:18:39.030
Please do your best.

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:51.000
You'll have to forgive
my difficult confederate.

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:53.210
You have my utmost sympathy.

00:18:53.210 --> 00:18:57.920
The two of them are joking,
but the mood is more tense than before.

00:18:57.920 --> 00:19:00.140
Once again, King Souma,

00:19:00.140 --> 00:19:04.600
I am General Jeanne Euphoria
of the Grand Chaos Empire.

00:19:04.600 --> 00:19:08.890
I am here representing Maria Euphoria.

00:19:08.890 --> 00:19:14.520
I welcome you, Jeanne. I am Souma Kazuya,
Acting King of Elfrieden.

00:19:14.520 --> 00:19:18.240
Princess Liscia,
I am relieved to find you well.

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:21.530
Jeanne, I am also most pleased
that you are doing well.

00:19:21.530 --> 00:19:23.910
Oh, you two know each other?

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:27.120
Yes. We met once when we were little.

00:19:27.120 --> 00:19:29.540
That was before the Demon
Lord's Domain appeared.

00:19:29.540 --> 00:19:34.420
Yes, it was. As I recall, it was a
conference with the former King Albert.

00:19:34.420 --> 00:19:37.920
Since we were the same age,
we played together.

00:19:39.260 --> 00:19:42.140
I would like to start having
a frank discussion now.

00:19:42.140 --> 00:19:44.890
I know. But before we begin,

00:19:44.890 --> 00:19:48.060
Liscia, would you go
and get Serina for me?

00:19:48.060 --> 00:19:49.480
All right.

00:19:54.980 --> 00:19:56.940
Oh, that reminds me.

00:19:56.940 --> 00:20:01.200
You mentioned playing together
with Liscia when you were little.

00:20:01.200 --> 00:20:04.660
I guess royal family members must
interact with each other a lot, huh?

00:20:04.660 --> 00:20:06.620
I don't know about other nations,

00:20:06.620 --> 00:20:11.080
but I forced the foreign minister to
take me along when I met the princess.

00:20:11.080 --> 00:20:12.620
Is that right?

00:20:12.620 --> 00:20:16.710
It looks as though Princess Liscia
has grown even stronger than before.

00:20:16.710 --> 00:20:18.880
If you say so.

00:20:18.880 --> 00:20:22.430
Even then, I couldn't land
a single hit on her.

00:20:22.430 --> 00:20:27.260
How did we go from talking about playing
together to landing hits on each other?

00:20:27.260 --> 00:20:29.640
You two must have been awfully tomboyish.

00:20:29.640 --> 00:20:33.600
Or are you just trying
to keep me in check?

00:20:33.600 --> 00:20:35.020
Maybe.

00:20:38.360 --> 00:20:41.650
I am here as requested, Your Majesty.

00:20:41.650 --> 00:20:47.120
Serina, the Amidonian prince
Julius is in the VIP suite.

00:20:47.120 --> 00:20:49.700
Would you start the banquet
and see that he is entertained?

00:20:49.700 --> 00:20:54.330
As you wish. Is it fair to say...

00:20:54.330 --> 00:20:56.750
...that you want me to <i>take charge </i>of him?

00:20:56.750 --> 00:21:00.670
You're so formal.
But yes, that's what I mean.

00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:04.380
Then, Your Majesty, I would like
permission to open the bottle

00:21:04.380 --> 00:21:07.350
of vintage tequeur
in the castle's wine cellar.

00:21:07.350 --> 00:21:10.810
As long as you provide your own level
of hospitality, that will be fine.

00:21:12.020 --> 00:21:17.190
Yes, sire. I will see to it that Julius
receives <i>bottle service </i>from me.

00:21:17.190 --> 00:21:22.860
I am sure that Julius will be pleased
with my hospitality, as well.

00:21:26.360 --> 00:21:28.950
What's the matter, you two?

00:21:33.830 --> 00:21:37.710
Souma, tequeur is a liquor
well known for its strength.

00:21:37.710 --> 00:21:40.710
It has an agreeable flavor,
so people end up drinking too much of it.

00:21:40.710 --> 00:21:42.340
If someone is not
accustomed to its effects,

00:21:42.340 --> 00:21:45.380
they will be on their way
to dreamland in no time.

00:21:45.380 --> 00:21:49.180
Then, if she serves him that drink...

00:21:49.180 --> 00:21:52.810
...the banquet will be over
in less than ten minutes.

00:21:52.810 --> 00:21:54.930
That's no hospitality at all!

00:22:00.820 --> 00:22:04.820
Just this once, I feel sorry for Julius.

00:22:06.320 --> 00:22:09.240
This really is quite the amusing country.

00:22:09.240 --> 00:22:13.790
Ahem, let's relocate
and start negotiating,

00:22:13.790 --> 00:22:18.330
Jeanne Euphoria, general of
the Gran Chaos Empire's forces.

00:22:18.330 --> 00:22:24.420
Of course, Provisional King Souma
Kazuya of the Kingdom of Elfrieden.

00:22:35.060 --> 00:22:39.100
<i>"What are we supposed to choose?"</i>

00:22:39.100 --> 00:22:44.360
<i>Our voices imploring the future are hoarse</i>

00:22:44.360 --> 00:22:50.450
<i>We've become so afraid</i>
<i>of what we could lose</i>

00:22:50.450 --> 00:22:55.410
<i>that we're just frozen in place</i>

00:22:55.410 --> 00:22:59.870
<i>How many times have we made mistakes</i>

00:22:59.870 --> 00:23:05.840
<i>because we wanted to check our "answers"?</i>

00:23:05.840 --> 00:23:13.180
<i>Before we knew it we were in love,</i>
<i>we had fallen in love</i>

00:23:13.180 --> 00:23:17.430
<i>I'll hold fast to you</i>
<i>in the times we're in</i>

00:23:17.430 --> 00:23:23.230
<i>We who set alight</i>
<i>our finite lives to fight</i>

00:23:23.230 --> 00:23:28.490
<i>are noble and beautiful above all</i>

00:23:28.490 --> 00:23:32.450
<i>As long as we create</i>
<i>as many bright tomorrows</i>

00:23:32.450 --> 00:23:37.790
<i>as the indelible wounds we suffer,</i>

00:23:37.790 --> 00:23:46.840
<i>we can be proud of all</i>
<i>we've woven together</i>
